objectives:
18.177 The objective, to which this subprogramme contributes, is to eradicate extreme poverty and reduce multidimensional poverty, by ensuring that members of ECA have evidence-based policies and strategies for social investment and productive job creation.
18.178 To contribute to the objective, the subprogramme will:
(a) Develop analytical knowledge, provide technical assistance and promote regional dialogue and learning for members of ECA on designing national social policies and strategies for reducing multidimensional poverty and provision of social protection to the most vulnerable;
(b) Generate knowledge, provide technical assistance to members of ECA and organize regional dialogues and learning initiatives on strategies to leverage migration for inclusive development in Africa;
(c) Develop analytical knowledge and provide technical assistance to members of ECA in the regional implementation and appraisal of global agreements, including the Global Compact for Safe, Orderly and Regular Migration, the Madrid International Plan of Action on Ageing, 2002, the Programme of Action of the International Conference on Population and Development and the Addis Ababa Declaration on Population and Development in Africa beyond 2014;
(d) Enhance knowledge and skills of members of ECA through technical assistance and regional policy learning and dialogues on youth employment to enhance job creation, leverage the demographic dividend and support social cohesion.
18.179 The above-mentioned work is expected to result in:
(a) Improved assessment and analysis by member States of poverty, with a focus on multidimensional poverty;
(b) Increased prioritization of productive job creation in national development planning, and strategies, policies and programmes, in order to accelerate the eradication of extreme poverty and reduction of multidimensional poverty;
(c) Enhanced, evidence-based policy options for the provision of social protection for the most vulnerable;
(d) Strengthened responses by members of ECA to address migration, population and development challenges and opportunities, including through youth employment policies and programmes.

